        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Black Friday is real but rarely the year's low for treadmills, because demand is about to
            rise rather than fall. <strong class="text-white">Model-year changeover and late spring
            are where the deep discounts live</strong> — and the price history, not the label, is
            the only thing that tells you which is which.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Decide the specification before the sale and watch only your shortlist. Then remember that
            <a href="/new-vs-used-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">buying used</a>
            and <a href="/best-treadmills-without-subscriptions/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">avoiding a subscription</a>
            each save more than any sale event will.
          </p>
        </div>
